course: dictionary
lesson: 10535
title: Ukrainian: a place, a person, a language
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word Ukrainian can work in three ways. As an adjective, it describes things from Ukraine, a large country in eastern Europe. As a noun, a Ukrainian is a person from Ukraine. It can also be the name of a language, the one spoken in Ukraine.
explain: Context tells you which meaning you have. «Pysanky are Ukrainian Easter eggs decorated with wax and dye» uses Ukrainian to describe the eggs, so it is an adjective. «Ukrainian has seven cases» names the language, so it is a noun.
explain: Ask yourself what word would fit. If you can put «the language» or «from Ukraine» into the sentence and it still makes sense, you have found the meaning. Always check the sentence, not just the word.
fact: Ukraine is a large country in eastern Europe.
fact: A Ukrainian is a person from Ukraine, and Ukrainians means more than one person.
fact: Ukrainian, the language, is a Slavic language written in the Cyrillic alphabet.
fact: «Pysanky» are Ukrainian Easter eggs decorated with wax and dye, with patterns like the sun, wheat or waves.
fact: The Ukrainian flag is blue and yellow.
exercise: «The Ukrainian flag is blue and yellow.» In this sentence, what does Ukrainian tell you about the flag? | It is very old | *It comes from Ukraine | It is blue and yellow | It is a language
exercise: «Many pupils at our school speak Ukrainian and English.» What does Ukrainian name here? | A flag | A country's food | A festival | *A language
exercise: What is a Ukrainian? | A kind of Easter egg | A large mountain | *A person from Ukraine | A Cyrillic letter
test: What are pysanky? | *Decorated Ukrainian Easter eggs | Ukrainian flags | Dances from a small village | Wax candles for a birthday
test: Which of these is a Ukrainian food, named in the lessons? | Curry | *Borscht | Pizza | Fish and chips
exam: «Ukrainian has seven cases; the vocative is the case for calling someone.» In this sentence, what does Ukrainian mean? | A country in Africa | A person from Ukraine | A flag | *The language
